{
  "_doc": "Painted floor per planet or biome id (src/world/groundPaint.ts). kind picks the surface detail: grass (blades, clover, flowers, leaves), snow (wind ridges, ice glints, sparkle), sand (ripples), spore (spongy pores, glowing specks), basalt (cracked plates with glowing seams), regolith (craters), salt (a dry salt pan: crust broken into polygons with raised pressure ridges, damp brine patches where cover lies, glints). soil = bare ground ramp dark to light, cover = what grows or lies on it (grass, snow, moss, ash), coverage = 0..1 how much of the floor it covers. detail = extra colors for the kind (blades, flowers, glow seams, specks). stone = ruin floor slabs. pebbles = per 10,000 px. relief = how strongly bumps are shaded. rock = painted outcrops (src/world/rockPaint.ts): ramp dark to light, cover (moss/snow in the hollows) + coverage, seams (glowing plate joints), cracks (contour crack density), relief (slope shading).",
